{
  "id": "world-challenge-2000",
  "name": "World Challenge 2000",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "World Challenge 2000 was Japan's official tournament season that year: a spring circuit of over 30 tournaments from 25 March to 10 June 2000, then World Challenge Summer, at eight venues from Yokohama on 1 and 2 July to Sendai on 6 August. Players got Lucky Stadium, made in eight regional versions, each with a landmark of its region behind a card-battle stadium, such as Mount Aso with Onix for Kyūshū or Tokyo Tower with Lugia for Kantō.\n\nWorld Challenge Summer decided who went to that year's Best in Japan finals, in two divisions: the junior Tropical Mega Battle and the senior Secret Super Battle. The top three of each division at each tournament won No. 1, No. 2 and No. 3 Trainer trophy cards, each in an acrylic case printed with the winner's name and region. Ken Sugimori drew them in a boy's and a girl's version, to match the winner, with more Pokémon the higher the place. Few girls placed, so the girls' versions are the rarer ones.",
    "sources": [
